// Why FRP was introduced?

// Before FRP, applications handled events using callbacks.

// Example:

// button.addEventListener("click", () => {
//     fetchData(() => {
//         updateUI();
//     });
// });

// When applications became larger:

// Too many callbacks
// Difficult to maintain
// Callback Hell
// Complex asynchronous logic
// Hard to combine multiple events

// FRP was introduced to solve these problems by treating events as streams of data.